[{"category":"section","location":"#ThreadSafeDicts.jl","page":"Home","text":"A thread-safe Dict type for Julia programming\n\n<br> <img src=\"https://github.com/wherrera10/ThreadSafeDicts.jl/blob/master/docs/src/spool.png\"> <br><br>","title":"ThreadSafeDicts.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Struct-and-Constructors","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Struct and Constructors"},{"category":"section","location":"#ThreadSafeDict","page":"Home","text":"struct ThreadSafeDict{K,V} <: AbstractDict{K,V}\n    dlock::ReentrantLock\n    d::Dict{K,V}\n    ThreadSafeDict{K,V}() where {K,V} = new(ReentrantLock(), Dict{K,V}())\n    ThreadSafeDict{K,V}(d::Dict{K,V}) where {K,V} =\n        new(ReentrantLock(), copy(d))\n    ThreadSafeDict{K,V}(itr) where {K,V} =\n        new(ReentrantLock(), Dict{K,V}(itr))\nend\n\nThreadSafeDict()\nThreadSafeDict(d::Dict{K,V}) where {K,V}\nThreadSafeDict(itr)\n\nStruct and constructors for ThreadSafeDict. There is one private ReentrantLock per Dict struct. All functions lock this lock, pass arguments to the d member Dict, unlock the ReentrantLock, and then return what is returned by the Dict.","title":"ThreadSafeDict"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(\"ThreadSafeDicts\")","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Functions-Reference","page":"Home","text":"This block automatically extracts docstrings from your source code:\n\n","title":"Functions Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"#ThreadSafeDicts.ThreadSafeDict","page":"Home","text":"ThreadSafeDict(pairs::Vector{Pair{K,V}})\n\nStruct and constructor for ThreadSafeDict. There is one lock per Dict struct. All functions lock this lock, pass  arguments to the d member Dict, unlock the spinlock, and then return what is returned by the Dict.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ThreadSafeDicts.ThreadSafeDict"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.delete!-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict, Any}","page":"Home","text":"delete!(dic::ThreadSafeDict, k)\n\ndelete key k and its value from the dict\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.delete!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.empty!-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict}","page":"Home","text":"empty!(dic::ThreadSafeDict)\n\nRemove all keys and values from the Dict\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.empty!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.get!-Tuple{Function, ThreadSafeDict, Any}","page":"Home","text":"get!(f::Function, dic::ThreadSafeDict, k)\n\nGet value at key k if exists, otherwise set value at k to f() and return that value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.get!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.get!-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"get!(dic::ThreadSafeDict, k, v)\n\nGet value at key k if exists, otherwise set value at k to v and return v.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.get!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.get-Tuple{Function, ThreadSafeDict, Any}","page":"Home","text":"get(f::Function, dic::ThreadSafeDict, k)\n\nGet value at key k if exists, otherwise return f()\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.get"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.get-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"get(dic::ThreadSafeDict, k, v)\n\nGet value at key k if exists, otherwise return v\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.get"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.getindex-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict, Any}","page":"Home","text":"getindex(dic::ThreadSafeDict, k)\n\nGet the value at key index k.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.getindex"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.haskey-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict, Any}","page":"Home","text":"haskey(dic::ThreadSafeDict, k)\n\nReturn true if key k is in the dict, else return false.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.haskey"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.iterate-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict, Any}","page":"Home","text":"iterate(dic::ThreadSafeDict, i)\n\nIterate through the Dict returning its key-value pairs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.iterate"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.iterate-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict}","page":"Home","text":"iterate(dic::ThreadSafeDict)\n\nIterate through the Dict returning its key-value pairs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.iterate"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.length-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict}","page":"Home","text":"length(dic::ThreadSafeDict)\n\nReturn the length of the Dict, considered as a vector of key-value pairs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.length"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.pop!-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict}","page":"Home","text":"pop!(dic::ThreadSafeDict)\n\nremove and return a key-value pair from the Dict\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.pop!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.print-Tuple{IO, ThreadSafeDict}","page":"Home","text":"print(io::IO, dic::ThreadSafeDict)\n\nPrint the ThreadSafeDict, including the state of its lock and contents of the undelying Dict.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.print"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.setindex!-Tuple{ThreadSafeDict, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"setindex!(dic::ThreadSafeDict, k, v)\n\nSet the value at key index k to v.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.setindex!"}]
